Z||000000||glava2876||06-21-2001||07:45 PM||||After getting my Fiero runing, the leaking brake line seemed like a little problem -NOT!I removed the line that goes from the master cylider to the spliter block at the rear brakes -not too tough. I even worked both rear bleeders free -great! Run down to the NAPA and pick up (2) 5' and (1) 2' 1/4" sections and conectors. I can't get the right fittings, but the old ones are fine so I remove them and contact my local mechanic to install them and "bubble" flare -easy -NO. He said that the NAPA lines are actually metric, even thogh the say 1/4" and he can't use his 1/4" die??? I know that probably everyone on here knows what to do -a brake line source you have used or the correct way to convert? Can someone please help me get this done. It took a couple of months to pull and clean the gas tank, install a new fuel pump and replace the TBI gaskets and "O" rings -I really want to dive this car! Thanks, Glen   ||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||06-21-2001||08:04 PM||||This is very common. Premade lines are only made in a few configurations. Cost to much to match every car. <P>They make all kinds of adaptor fittings for just this problem. You may have to take the MC or whatever with you to get the right adaprots.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SteveJ||06-21-2001||08:05 PM||||Bought mine at Autozone and they sold me an adapter for each end. Problem solved.||||reg||1
